good afternoon ketanji brown jackson  would be the first black woman to serve  on the u.s supreme court if confirmed  the daughter of school teachers who  themselves had attended segregated  schools  jackson was once advised by a high  school counselor that harvard university  was out of reach it wasn't she graduated  with top honors and stay to study law  the beginning of a brilliant legal  career  i can only hope that my life and career  my love of this country and the  constitution  and my commitment to upholding the rule  of law and the sacred principles upon  which this great nation was founded  will inspire future generations of  americans i think having  judge jackson as justice jackson will  really open up to  so many more people in the united states  and around the world to the possibility  that there aren't limitations and that  if there are little girls all around the  country who say one day i'd like to be  on the highest court of the land they  can look at justice jackson and know  that that is an entirely probable path  for them  jackson is currently serving on the  federal court of appeals for the d.c  circuit she's been there for only a few  months nominated by biden and confirmed  by the u.s senate in june in a vote that  included yeses from three republicans  the white house is hoping for a repeat  performance her opinions are always  carefully reasoned  tethered to precedent and demonstrate  reflect respect for how the law impacts  everyday people jackson has a record as  a liberal jurist in 2019 as a district  court judge she blocked president  trump's attempts to shield a former  white house aide from testifying before  congress famously writing presidents are  not kings  she's also worked as a federal public  defender once assigned to represent an  afghan guantanamo bay detainee among  other people accused of crimes but  unable to pay for their own defense  i think that  that perspective will allow her to have  an insight into  the human element of of cases which none  of the other justices will obviously  share because none of them have this  this experience president biden is  looking for a swift confirmation in the  evenly divided senate where a simple  majority will be needed and likely  delivered that's despite criticism from  some prominent republicans like senate  minority leader mitch mcconnell who  claims jackson is the favored choice of  far left dark money groups  if confirmed jackson would replace  another liberal justice stephen breyer  when he retires this summer that would  leave the supreme court's 6-3 majority  unchanged but at age 51 jackson has the  potential to serve for decades on the  high court and adding a historic win to  biden's legacy thank you all heidi joe  castro al jazeera washington
 

